<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  RoviaFreeDev: the UI-only development build for a free Apple Personal Team.

  This file is deliberately empty. Every entitlement in the full build maps
  to a capability a Personal Team provisioning profile cannot carry:

  - com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension (packet-tunnel-provider)
    is the restricted entitlement a NEPacketTunnelProvider needs, and the
    reason the real RoviaTunnel.appex requires a paid Apple Developer Program
    membership. This target embeds no extension at all.
  - com.apple.security.application-groups needs an App Group registered on
    the App ID, which the developer portal only offers to paid members.
    Without it the app falls back to its own container, which the code
    already handles (RoviaApp.makeSubscriptionCoordinator,
    KeychainAccessGroup.resolve treats "no shared group" as "no sharing").
  - keychain-access-groups would pin the shared Keychain group; the probe in
    KeychainAccessGroup.resolve degrades to the app's default group instead.

  An entitlement a profile does not authorise is an install failure, not a
  warning, so the honest UI-only build asks for nothing. VPN actions are
  disabled in code under ROVIA_UI_ONLY; this plist is what makes the build
  signable, the code is what makes it truthful.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
